{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1426836-ecology-in-scion","id":1426836,"title":"Ecology in Scion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-01T10:36:06-08:00","id":1426836,"title":"Ecology in Scion","content":"What could be possible ecological implications of Scion World? Am I only one thinking that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climate_change\" target=\"_blank\">Climate Change</a> we have over our heads can lead to new Titanomachy, with ancient spells being broken by changing climate, letting free Titans from previous prisons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-01-2020, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T12:18:49-08:00","id":1426846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1426836-ecology-in-scion#post1426836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What could be possible ecological implications of Scion World? Am I only one thinking that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climate_change\" target=\"_blank\">Climate Change</a> we have over our heads can lead to new Titanomachy, with ancient spells being broken by changing climate, letting free Titans in previous prisons?</div> </div> </div> </div>The conceit of the World is, of course, that it is not visibly very different from our world, so I don't think that its ecology is significantly different - <i>yet</i>. However, that is exactly the kind of thing that can change over the course of a game. Climate change loosening the bonds of the Titans is certainly poetic, but seeing as so many Titans' &quot;prisons&quot; are not physical, I wouldn't focus on that aspect too much. Rather, I wonder how climate change could sway the opinions of deities that have so far been on &quot;our side.&quot; There are plenty of deities depicted as being on the fence about humanity or favouring nature and animals over humanity already. The ecological disaster we are currently creating could inspire a lot of figures to turn against humanity, it could split whole Pantheons on the question. There's a lot of potential in that, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T17:50:27-08:00","id":1426887,"title":"","content":"Everything in the sea is eaten by sharkfolk. The end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T00:23:02-08:00","id":1427115,"title":"","content":"There's a couple of mentions of this in the various gods write-ups. Poseidon, for example, is really pissed at the state of the seas in the modern age and he only hasn't obliterated a city or two because Zeus forbids it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23975-pxgentleman","name":"PXGentleman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T02:18:33-08:00","id":1427118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PXGentleman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1426836-ecology-in-scion?p=1427115#post1427115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a couple of mentions of this in the various gods write-ups. Poseidon, for example, is really pissed at the state of the seas in the modern age and he only hasn't obliterated a city or two because Zeus forbids it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, if that isn't a good basis for a Pantheon splitting, even going to war with each other, over the issue of ecology <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Poseidon and Zeus have enough tension already, throw in rapidly rising sea temperatures and pollution, and a certain god may consider repeating his previous coup attempt <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T04:51:51-08:00","id":1427125,"title":"","content":"One thing that ecological awareness could set up is pantheon splits and civil wars among even pantheons who agree about how serious the ecological crises are. Example from the real world, the Inuit peoples on the whole are onboard with ecological awareness and the need to protect/nurture the environment (there are exceptions in every group). Still, whale hunting is sacred. The conflict becomes obvious. <br /> <br /> Throughout the planet there are similar issues if you look for them. Decent people caught between vital and irreconcilable needs and imperatives. The possibilities of drama are rich.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}